<title>TURKEY: Turkey central bank reserves hit high in latest wk.</title>
<headline>Turkey central bank reserves hit high in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose by $69 million to a record high of $17.332 billion in the week ending on October 4.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>		   Oct 4	  Sept 27	end-1995</p>
<p> Forex reserve  17.332	 17.263	  12.391</p>
<p> Gold reserve    1.383	  1.383	   1.383</p>
<p> Total reserve  18.715	 18.646	  13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $27 million to $27.683 billion in the week ending September 20, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
